%description:

Tcp.windowAutoTuning:on -- the offer grows above the advertised window.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "receive window auto-tuning, as Linux (tcp_grow_window()): the offered
window starts at advertisedWindow and grows with each received data segment toward a clamp of
half the receive buffer; needs receiveBufferSize, else an error".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true, the value of LinuxTcp), no-buffer (true
without receiveBufferSize: an error). The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() sets
the offer and the clamp, half the buffer, and checks the buffer; each data segment grows the
offer by max(2 * MSS, 2 * its length) up to the clamp (TcpConnection::processSegment1stThru8th()). This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host2, with an advertised window of 16384 bytes and a receive buffer of 131072
bytes (preconditions), whose application reads at once; host1 sends 1000000 bytes. Observation: level 2, until 2 s, the send window of host1 (the signal sndWnd) grows above
40000 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowAutoTuning
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.windowAutoTuning
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpWindowAutoTuningOn")
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("sndWnd")
                                        .captureMax("largestWindow", "value")
                                        .within(3.0)))
        .act(action().at(2.0)
                 .describe("the largest send window of host1 until 2 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "{largestWindow} > 40000"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowAutoTuningOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.windowAutoTuning = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 16384
*.host2.tcp.receiveBufferSize = 131072B
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpWindowAutoTuningOn: PASS
